        "content": "Given:\n- First wing: 9 floors, 6 halls per floor, 32 rooms per hall.\n- Second wing: 7 floors, 9 halls per floor, 40 rooms per hall.\n\nUnknown: Total number of rooms in the hotel.\n\nTo find the total number of rooms, we need to calculate the number of rooms in each wing and then sum them up.\n\nFor the first wing:\n- Number of floors = 9\n- Number of halls per floor = 6\n- Number of rooms per hall = 32\n- Total rooms in the first wing = 9 floors * 6 halls/floor * 32 rooms/hall = 1728 rooms\n\nFor the second wing:\n- Number of floors = 7\n- Number of halls per floor = 9\n- Number of rooms per hall = 40\n- Total rooms in the second wing = 7 floors * 9 halls/floor * 40 rooms/hall = 2520 rooms\n\nTotal rooms in the hotel = Rooms in the first wing + Rooms in the second wing\n= 1728 + 2520 = 4248 rooms\n\nThe previous answer of 1800 rooms was incorrect. The correct total number of rooms in the hotel is 4248.\n\nFINAL: 4248",
